      "repair_reason": "- [P1] The code blocker is a narrow mechanical repair, although the contributor must still provide real behavior proof before merge.; Needs attention: The strict parser improves validation, but its malformed-response path currently omits stream cancellation and introduces a low-severity availability concern.; Review finding: [P2] Cancel malformed response bodies before throwing — src/infra/clawhub.ts:823 (sha=61e152ec49c27b7d977b2c4966a29e4d36e60b8c)",
      "review_summary": "Replaces ClawHub response Content-Length parsing with the shared strict media parser for identity-encoded responses.\n\nPR surface: Source -2. Total -2 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. at source level: an invalid identity Content-Length makes parseMediaContentLength throw before response.body.cancel can execute. No live current-head response transcript was supplied.",
